# Ashiok, Dream Render: a search it forbids is not a search (CR 101.2, 701.23), so "whenever an opponent searches their
# library" (Wan Shi Tong, Librarian, also Bot1's) does not see it. Bot1 casts Ashiok and a Wan Shi Tong with X = 0 on turn 1. Bot2's Demonic
# Tutor on turn 2 is forbidden: no counter. Bot1's own Winds of Abandon on turn 3 exiles Bot2's Ornithopter, and Bot2 searches
# for a basic land on Bot1's spell (allowed): one counter, so the two differ only in whose spell it was.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Ashiok, Dream Render
Wan Shi Tong, Librarian
Winds of Abandon
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Demonic Tutor
Island x3
Lightning Bolt
Plains
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Hand.Ashiok, Dream Render.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Wan Shi Tong, Librarian.Cast(X: 0)
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Demonic Tutor.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Wan Shi Tong, Librarian.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Winds of Abandon.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Search(Plains)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Wan Shi Tong, Librarian.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot2.Graveyard = Demonic Tutor
